  "notes": "Sheet 0 (Anantara Mina Al Arab, Ras Al Khaimah, the emirate's first overwater villas, on a private peninsula among mangroves): each villa is a white rendered box raised on white piles over the lagoon, under a steep thatched hip roof with deep eaves; a glazed front onto a timber deck with a dark balustrade and a raised plunge pool on the white platform; a long timber jetty runs past them on a line of piles and spurs lead to each; one villa stands in a revetment of grey boulders; the aerial shows three villas in a row beside the mangrove shore (grey-green, low round crowns on pale sand). Modelled: the lagoon plate, three villas on a straight jetty with their spurs, boulders under the middle one, a mangrove bank and sandbar on the east edge, two palms. Not modelled: the resort's main building, spa and beach (the article shows only interiors of the villas and lobby - sheet 0, sheet 1 - none of the beach buildings), and the aerial's curve of the jetty. Guessed: the villa size (about 10 m square, from the deck against a person and the aerial), the spacing, the number of villas actually in a row. A public resort; its spot is the resort's own point (OpenStreetMap, via Nominatim); only the villas are drawn here, not the whole peninsula."
